    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For two equal distances, there is a useful shortcut.\n\nIf the speeds are x and y:\nAverage speed = 2xy ÷ (x + y).\n\nFor 30 and 60 km/hr:\n2 × 30 × 60 ÷ 90 = 40 km/hr.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Why the harmonic formula works:\n\nUse the same distance d for each leg.\nTime = d/x + d/y.\nAverage = 2d ÷ [d/x + d/y].\nThe d cancels, leaving 2xy/(x+y).",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
